      hornLength: "Bull: Average 33-38 inches (generally shorter due to wear from fighting). Cow: Average 36-42+ inches (often longer than bulls). This reversal of typical sexual dimorphism presents unique challenge for trophy hunting - females often outscore bulls in record books because scoring system prioritizes length over mass. SCI Gold Medal Standard: ~40 inches. Rowland Ward Minimum: 40 inches.",
