      primaryForage: "Gemsbok are grazers that can dig for water, accessing resources unavailable to other species. They are expert locators of water-bearing plants such as wild tsamma melon (Citrullus lanatus) and gemsbok cucumber (Acanthosicyos naudinianus) - these fruits can consist of over 90% water. During droughts, will dig up to meter into sand to access nutritious and moisture-rich roots and tubers, behavior not commonly seen in other large antelope. They act as seed dispersers for tsamma melon and other desert plants. Can process coarse desert vegetation when grazing.",
