        distinctive: "Splayed toes function like snowshoe, reducing ground pressure for loose sand. Used as spades to dig up succulent roots. Bull vs. Cow: Distinguishing sex by track alone difficult but possible for expert trackers. Bull tracks tend to be blunter at tips and blockier, with heavier impression due to greater body mass. Cow tracks may appear slightly more tapered and slender. In deep sand, tracks connected by drag marks where animal doesn't lift feet high - depth of drag marks indicates fatigue",
