        "Desert adaptation - can allow body to hyperthermic (45°C) while protecting brain through selective brain cooling",
        "Defensive posture - lowers hindquarters and keeps head low, presenting horns as barrier",
        "Active predator defense - will stand and fight, impaling lions, leopards, and hyenas",
        "Root excavation - digs up to meter into sand to access roots and tubers during droughts",
        "Dominance displays - standing broadside to maximize size profile, holding head high and arching neck",
        "Sparring - 'fencing' with horns to test strength (common), serious fighting (rare but violent)",
