        "Loud roars during rut - guttural, pig-like grunting and snorting sequence, often mistaken for leopard or lion",
        "The explosion - when predator detected, herd explodes in all directions, scattering effect",
        "Stotting/pronking - high, vertical bounds intended to demonstrate fitness to predator",
        "The string jump - bowhunter's nemesis, animal drops body 10-20cm when hearing bow release",
        "Tail flagging - when fleeing, tail raised flashing white underside while black stripes provide high-contrast visual reference",
