      shotPlacement: "CRITICAL: Improper shot placement is leading cause of lost trophies. The 'Hump' Illusion: Wildebeest have pronounced dorsal hump and high withers. Hunters accustomed to deer often aim too high, putting bullet into non-vital dorsal spines (the 'void') - paralyzes animal momentarily ('spinal shock') but recovers and runs off, often never to be found. Rule: Aim low. The Golden Triangle: Ideal shot is on vertical line of foreleg, one-third of way up body - hits top of heart and lungs. Quartering away: Aim for off-side shoulder - drives bullet through liver and lungs, lodging against far shoulder blade. Frontal shot: Only recommended with heavy calibers - aim for 'soft spot' at base of neck where it joins chest.",
